# Adhere strictly to the specified JSON output schema: (preference)

Standing user preference: Adhere strictly to the specified JSON output schema: compute the Domain Trust Score using the exact formula components (Domain_Age_Score, SSL_Validity, DNS_Consistency, Metadata_Integrity) and their defined weights; apply the -15 point WHOIS privacy deduction; use the exact enum literals for status, integrity, and risk_level fields; state 'MISSING' for any unavailable metadata field; and always include next_agent_notes with both to_FCA and to_AO keys.

## Conventions
- Adhere strictly to the specified JSON output schema: compute the Domain Trust Score using the exact formula components (Domain_Age_Score, SSL_Validity, DNS_Consistency, Metadata_Integrity) and their defined weights; apply the -15 point WHOIS privacy deduction; use the exact enum literals for status, integrity, and risk_level fields; state 'MISSING' for any unavailable metadata field; and always include next_agent_notes with both to_FCA and to_AO keys.

